1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,875
Bubble, I demand an apology!

2
00:00:01,875 --> 00:00:03,000
Huh? What for?

3
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,666
You know exactly the reason.
I know you do!

4
00:00:06,083 --> 00:00:07,250
Is it because I killed you?

5
00:00:07,250 --> 00:00:10,458
No! I don't care about that.
It's because you didn't give me IMMUNITY!

6
00:00:10,458 --> 00:00:14,708
What? That's it? Sorry, Flower,
but I don't think I'll apologize for that!

7
00:00:14,791 --> 00:00:15,500
You have to!

8
00:00:15,625 --> 00:00:17,250
Bubble, I-I'll apologize for you.

9
00:00:17,541 --> 00:00:21,250
F- uh, Flower, Bubble is sincerely sorry
for not giving you immunity.

10
00:00:21,416 --> 00:00:22,875
I-I guess that's adequate.

11
00:00:23,291 --> 00:00:26,750
OMG, Leafy! Why did you do that?
I thought you hated me!

12
00:00:26,750 --> 00:00:29,708
Well, I decided a little argument
shouldn't end our friendship.

13
00:00:29,750 --> 00:00:30,166
Oh.

14
00:00:30,166 --> 00:00:31,291
So let's be friends again!

15
00:00:31,291 --> 00:00:33,708
Leafy, we're friends, and then we're not,

16
00:00:33,708 --> 00:00:35,291
and then we're friends, and then we're not!

17
00:00:35,291 --> 00:00:37,791
Th-this doesn't seem like a very stable friendship.

18
00:00:37,791 --> 00:00:39,541
Oh, so now you don't want to be friends!

19
00:00:39,541 --> 00:00:41,916
- Oh?
- Well, I guess I'd rather be with Firey!

20
00:00:41,916 --> 00:00:43,625
At least he appreciates my presence.

21
00:00:43,791 --> 00:00:50,416
[INTRO PLAYS]

22
00:00:50,416 --> 00:00:51,416
Subtitles: TAFFYMARZI

23
00:00:53,625 --> 00:00:55,666
You know, Firey, I've never been
in a Ferris Wheel before.

24
00:00:55,666 --> 00:00:58,375
Wait till you get to the fun, special part!

25
00:00:58,375 --> 00:00:59,416
Ooh! Special?

26
00:00:59,416 --> 00:01:00,875
You go through a waterfall!

27
00:01:01,125 --> 00:01:02,541
You're... you're allergic to water.

28
00:01:02,541 --> 00:01:04,708
Yeah, I replaced with a lavafall.

29
00:01:04,958 --> 00:01:05,458
Uhh...

30
00:01:05,625 --> 00:01:08,625
Heh, heh, heh! Isn't this great?

31
00:01:08,625 --> 00:01:09,958
No! Get me outta this thing!

32
00:01:09,958 --> 00:01:13,000
Oh my gosh. Leafy, just calm
down and enjoy the ride!

33
00:01:13,083 --> 00:01:14,041
Ahhhh!

34
00:01:14,291 --> 00:01:15,958
When are we gonna do Cake at Stake?

35
00:01:15,958 --> 00:01:16,708
Right now.

36
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:18,875
♪ The points are gone ♪

37
00:01:18,875 --> 00:01:20,708
♪ We are free of them now ♪

38
00:01:20,708 --> 00:01:22,000
♪ But we look on ♪

39
00:01:23,125 --> 00:01:25,208
♪ To the moment that we see ♪

40
00:01:25,583 --> 00:01:27,416
♪ The next slice of cake ♪

41
00:01:27,750 --> 00:01:29,875
♪ A step closer to the prize ♪

42
00:01:29,875 --> 00:01:31,708
♪ Brought on by Cake at Stake ♪

43
00:01:33,833 --> 00:01:34,833
Oh my gosh! It's a bug!

44
00:01:35,916 --> 00:01:36,916
I-is it gone?

45
00:01:36,916 --> 00:01:38,500
Hey, wait! Where's Leafy?

46
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:40,000
She died in the ferris wheel.

47
00:01:40,208 --> 00:01:43,791
Yeah, I-I know that. But won't the
Master Recovery Center create her again?

48
00:01:43,833 --> 00:01:47,041
We had to sell the recovery
centers because of budget cuts.

49
00:01:47,250 --> 00:01:49,000
- You didn't! You couldn't have!
- Wanna bet?

50
00:01:49,250 --> 00:01:50,375
Actually I do.

51
00:01:50,375 --> 00:01:51,083
How much?

52
00:01:51,083 --> 00:01:52,375
My life's earnings.

53
00:01:52,375 --> 00:01:55,333
Well, it turns out that we
actually did sell them,

54
00:01:55,333 --> 00:01:56,541
so thanks for the money.

55
00:01:56,625 --> 00:01:59,041
So wait, you really sold the recovery centers?

56
00:01:59,041 --> 00:02:00,625
You mean Leafy's never coming back?!

57
00:02:00,625 --> 00:02:02,333
Yep. Can we move on now?

58
00:02:02,416 --> 00:02:03,958
No! I want Leafy back!

59
00:02:03,958 --> 00:02:06,916
Whatever. Be quiet. Now we really have to get going.

60
00:02:06,916 --> 00:02:09,166
I agree, let's get to the elimination!

61
00:02:09,166 --> 00:02:11,000
We have something else to get to first.

62
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:11,958
Really? What?

63
00:02:11,958 --> 00:02:13,458
You seriously don't remember?

64
00:02:13,541 --> 00:02:16,083
Sorry. Bubbles don't have brains. Give me a hint!

65
00:02:16,083 --> 00:02:18,708
It has to do with the cancellation of BFDI.

66
00:02:18,708 --> 00:02:20,791
Hmm... I give up. Tell me!

67
00:02:20,791 --> 00:02:24,833
If the number of votes go down yet again,
BFDI will be cancelled.

68
00:02:24,833 --> 00:02:26,500
Oh my gosh! I hope that doesn't happen!

69
00:02:26,500 --> 00:02:27,458
Let's find out.

70
00:02:31,041 --> 00:02:32,583
This suspense is KILLING me!

71
00:02:33,708 --> 00:02:35,375
Hey guys! For a prank,

72
00:02:35,375 --> 00:02:38,000
place an Announcer Recovery Center
next to a trampoline.

73
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:41,958
Then throw Spongy onto the trampoline.
After that, kill the Announcer!

74
00:02:41,958 --> 00:02:44,625
It's a fun, easy way to create the ultimate prank!

75
00:02:44,625 --> 00:02:51,083
Voiceover:
This program, was brought to you by
Blocky's Funny Doings International.

76
00:02:51,708 --> 00:02:54,916
Please donate money to the
No More Advertisements Foundation

77
00:02:54,916 --> 00:02:57,666
to prevent ads like these
from appearing in TV Shows.

78
00:02:57,875 --> 00:03:01,916
We think ads are boring, frustrating,
disgusting and irritating.

79
00:03:02,250 --> 00:03:03,208
Don't you too?!

80
00:03:03,541 --> 00:03:06,625
If you donate one dollar,
you'll get a bumper sticker.

81
00:03:06,625 --> 00:03:09,708
Donate five dollars and you'll
receive our subscription magazine

82
00:03:09,708 --> 00:03:12,958
which includes loads of
information on latest products.

83
00:03:13,375 --> 00:03:18,666
Donate a hundred dollars, and we'll put your name
in our next movie called "The Fight Against Commercials."

84
00:03:18,666 --> 00:03:20,125
Go check that one out, too!

85
00:03:20,333 --> 00:03:22,375
It's time to end advertisements.

86
00:04:05,708 --> 00:04:06,250
Huh?

87
00:04:06,250 --> 00:04:11,916
I'm sorry guys, but we got fewer
votes than last time, again. BFDI is cancelled.

88
00:04:11,958 --> 00:04:13,500
So, who wins Dream Island?

89
00:04:13,583 --> 00:04:14,291
No one does.

90
00:04:14,333 --> 00:04:16,125
No way! This is unacceptable!

91
00:04:16,208 --> 00:04:16,750
Why not?

92
00:04:16,875 --> 00:04:18,125
Because I want Dream Island!

93
00:04:18,208 --> 00:04:21,541
Well, too bad, and I don't think
you deserve it anyway.

94
00:04:21,625 --> 00:04:22,125
Grrr!

95
00:04:22,708 --> 00:04:24,000
What did you just throw on me?

96
00:04:24,125 --> 00:04:25,583
Uh, I don't know! Why does it matter?

97
00:04:25,750 --> 00:04:26,916
I think they're bug eggs.

98
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:27,500
Uh...

99
00:04:28,375 --> 00:04:29,208
Oh my Gardener!

100
00:04:30,958 --> 00:04:32,916
We have to run away people,
they'll eat us alive!

101
00:04:32,916 --> 00:04:35,208
Everyone:
Ahhhh!

102
00:04:39,875 --> 00:04:43,416
- What did you hear?
- Uhh... I-I  can't exactly tell what's going on right now,

103
00:04:43,416 --> 00:04:45,708
but I did hear him say that BFDI was cancelled.

104
00:04:45,708 --> 00:04:47,166
Oh my gosh! That's great!

105
00:04:47,166 --> 00:04:48,000
How so?

106
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:50,791
Well, if BFDI is over, that
means we should be released!

107
00:04:50,791 --> 00:04:51,916
Huh, that's true.

108
00:04:52,083 --> 00:04:54,625
Pen's right, I can hear footsteps right now!

109
00:04:54,625 --> 00:04:56,000
Wow, I can't wait!

110
00:05:03,250 --> 00:05:05,708
Oh my Bubble Blower, all the losers are dead!

111
00:05:05,708 --> 00:05:06,750
We have to keep going!

112
00:05:06,958 --> 00:05:14,541
Recommended Characters:
Ahhhhhh!

113
00:05:14,625 --> 00:05:16,750
Everyone:
Ahhhhh!

114
00:05:16,750 --> 00:05:18,083
What do we do about that canyon?

115
00:05:18,083 --> 00:05:18,750
Jump over it!

116
00:05:18,875 --> 00:05:19,375
Gah!

117
00:05:21,375 --> 00:05:22,666
Yes! I'm gonna make it!

118
00:05:25,291 --> 00:05:26,458
Flower:
Ahhhhh!

119
00:05:27,583 --> 00:05:29,875
Hey Firey, try burning the bugs.

120
00:05:29,875 --> 00:05:30,666
That won't work.

121
00:05:30,666 --> 00:05:31,583
Just try!

122
00:05:31,583 --> 00:05:32,166
G-geh...

123
00:05:32,958 --> 00:05:33,458
Uh oh.

124
00:05:34,375 --> 00:05:36,416
Oh no, Firey's been eaten!

125
00:05:36,416 --> 00:05:37,333
Just keep going.

126
00:05:55,833 --> 00:05:57,208
It's not killing all of them!

127
00:05:57,208 --> 00:05:59,875
Of course not, I built them to be strong.

128
00:05:59,875 --> 00:06:01,666
Wait, YOU built the bugs?

129
00:06:01,666 --> 00:06:03,666
Oops, forget I said anything.

130
00:06:03,666 --> 00:06:04,541
I can't believe-

131
00:06:04,875 --> 00:06:08,916
I have to keep my secrets.
Well, I guess it's time to do this.

132
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:15,458
Umm. I'm not sure what to do now,
because all of the contestants are gone.

133
00:06:15,458 --> 00:06:17,000
David:
Aw, seriously?!

134
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:20,333
Except for David of course,
because he's immune to bugs.

135
00:06:20,708 --> 00:06:22,416
Hey, I have a David Cloner.

136
00:06:24,291 --> 00:06:26,791
I decided to not cancel BFDI.

137
00:06:26,791 --> 00:06:28,333
David:
Aw, seriously?

138
00:06:28,333 --> 00:06:30,583
The cake this time is a red velvet cake.

139
00:06:30,583 --> 00:06:32,125
David:
Aw, seriously?

140
00:06:32,125 --> 00:06:35,750
It was recommended by "TotalDramaIsland5543."

141
00:06:35,750 --> 00:06:37,208
David:
Aw, seriously?

142
00:06:37,208 --> 00:06:39,208
Go subscribe to his or her channel.

143
00:06:39,208 --> 00:06:40,708
David:
Aw, seriously?

144
00:06:41,083 --> 00:06:42,791
There are 3 slices of cake.

145
00:06:42,791 --> 00:06:44,291
David:
Aw, seriously?

146
00:06:44,375 --> 00:06:47,125
3 contestants are safe and will get cake.

147
00:06:47,125 --> 00:06:48,583
David:
Aw, seriously?

148
00:06:48,583 --> 00:06:50,458
1 contestant will be eliminated.

149
00:06:50,458 --> 00:06:51,958
David:
Aw, seriously?

150
00:06:51,958 --> 00:06:54,125
Bubble had immunity, so she is safe.

151
00:06:54,125 --> 00:06:55,666
Aw, seriously?

152
00:06:56,291 --> 00:07:02,041
Out of the 735 votes, Firey got only 86,
so he's also safe.

153
00:07:02,041 --> 00:07:03,500
David:
Aw, seriously?

154
00:07:04,791 --> 00:07:06,708
Now it's down to Flower and Leafy.

155
00:07:06,708 --> 00:07:08,250
Aw, seriously?

156
00:07:11,666 --> 00:07:13,958
Announcer:
Leafy is safe with 125 votes.

157
00:07:14,083 --> 00:07:14,958
Aw, seriously?

158
00:07:16,708 --> 00:07:20,416
And Flower is eliminated with a record of 524 votes.

159
00:07:20,500 --> 00:07:21,333
What? No way!

160
00:07:21,333 --> 00:07:23,791
Oh my gosh, how did you people come back?

161
00:07:23,958 --> 00:07:25,666
We faked our deaths, obviously.

162
00:07:25,791 --> 00:07:26,333
Whatever.

163
00:07:26,500 --> 00:07:30,625
Announcer:
Flower, you're the first and last person to
be eliminated before the finale.

164
00:07:31,125 --> 00:07:34,000
- You, Flower, are out with four votes.
- Grrrr!

165
00:07:36,583 --> 00:07:38,666
Ahhhhh!

166
00:07:38,875 --> 00:07:39,458
Spongy...

167
00:07:39,458 --> 00:07:41,458
Ahhhhhh!

168
00:07:41,458 --> 00:07:42,958
...is eliminated at 4 votes.

169
00:07:43,083 --> 00:07:43,666
Ahh...

170
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:48,375
Blocky...

171
00:07:48,375 --> 00:07:50,416
Ahhhhh!

172
00:07:50,416 --> 00:07:52,000
...is eliminated at 6 votes.

173
00:07:52,083 --> 00:07:52,666
Ahh...

174
00:07:52,916 --> 00:07:55,000
Ahhhhh!

175
00:07:55,416 --> 00:07:56,125
- Woody...
- Ahh...

176
00:07:56,125 --> 00:07:57,666
...is eliminated at 9 votes.

177
00:07:57,666 --> 00:07:59,583
Ahhhhh!

178
00:07:59,750 --> 00:08:01,083
Ahhhhhhhhh!

179
00:08:01,333 --> 00:08:02,333
Goodbye, Pin.

180
00:08:02,333 --> 00:08:03,583
I use my Win Token!

181
00:08:03,583 --> 00:08:04,208
Announcer:
Too late!

182
00:08:04,208 --> 00:08:06,208
But I'm the team leader! You can't do that!

183
00:08:06,583 --> 00:08:07,125
Oh no!

184
00:08:07,416 --> 00:08:09,916
Eraser, you need a heroic leader like ME!

185
00:08:11,500 --> 00:08:12,000
And Needy...

186
00:08:12,208 --> 00:08:13,125
...is at 12 votes.

187
00:08:13,125 --> 00:08:17,583
Yeah but... Needle, why don't
you like being called "Needy?"

188
00:08:17,958 --> 00:08:18,458
Needy-

189
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:21,916
Teardrop, it's time to say goodbye.

190
00:08:24,375 --> 00:08:27,208
Goodbye, Golf Ball, or GBGB for short.

191
00:08:27,208 --> 00:08:30,291
Hyuck Hyuck, that's so hilare!

192
00:08:30,375 --> 00:08:40,750
Now my chances of winning
went from 7.143%, to 0.000%!

193
00:08:41,875 --> 00:08:43,916
Coiny, it looks like it's the end for you.

194
00:08:46,500 --> 00:08:51,541
Announcer:
Snowball, I'm sorry to tell you that
you've been eliminated with a record of 47 votes.

195
00:08:51,541 --> 00:08:52,500
Grrrr!

196
00:08:55,666 --> 00:08:57,458
NOOOOO...

197
00:08:57,458 --> 00:08:59,375
...OOOOOO-

198
00:09:01,458 --> 00:09:05,291
No, Match, no! You've been eliminated!

199
00:09:05,291 --> 00:09:10,583
OMG, I know it's so, like, hard,
but you got to keep, like, like, going!

200
00:09:10,583 --> 00:09:13,541
You got to win this for like, like,
like, like, the both of us!

201
00:09:15,250 --> 00:09:16,666
Eraser, goodbye.

202
00:09:18,666 --> 00:09:19,875
Pen will be eliminated.

203
00:09:22,333 --> 00:09:27,625
Blocky, I'm sorry, but you received 112 votes.
That's enough to eliminate you, again.

204
00:09:27,625 --> 00:09:31,625
No! You can't eliminate me!
I-I'm like the star of the show!

205
00:09:33,458 --> 00:09:35,000
Tennis Ball is eliminated.

206
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:36,000
Tennis Ball:
Ahhhhh!

207
00:09:38,625 --> 00:09:42,750
Announcer:
You received 259 votes, which is the most ever.
You are eliminated.

208
00:09:42,833 --> 00:09:45,583
What?! This machine thingy must be broken!

209
00:09:47,833 --> 00:09:48,916
David is eliminated.

210
00:09:49,041 --> 00:09:50,541
Aw, seriously?

211
00:09:51,708 --> 00:09:53,375
Ice Cube, you have been eliminated.

212
00:09:53,708 --> 00:09:54,500
Ahhhh!

213
00:09:54,750 --> 00:09:56,833
And Rocky is eliminated!

214
00:09:58,333 --> 00:09:59,125
- Spongy,
- Bwuh?

215
00:09:59,125 --> 00:10:03,000
with a record of 432 votes,
you have been eliminated, again.

216
00:10:04,166 --> 00:10:07,375
Well, I am not gonna be eliminated!
I've got my mirror!

217
00:10:08,333 --> 00:10:08,833
Ha!

218
00:10:12,125 --> 00:10:14,000
Why is there a bush here?

219
00:10:14,916 --> 00:10:15,416
Ha!

220
00:10:18,625 --> 00:10:19,958
It's so bright!

221
00:10:20,791 --> 00:10:21,291
Hah!

222
00:10:23,041 --> 00:10:24,125
Eliminated Contestants:
Yeah!

223
00:10:24,791 --> 00:10:26,666
Eliminated Contestants:
Ahhhhh!

224
00:10:33,791 --> 00:10:35,375
Oh no, not here again!

225
00:10:35,375 --> 00:10:37,583
So now we have our 3 finalists:

226
00:10:37,750 --> 00:10:39,416
Bubble, Firey and Leafy.

227
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:42,708
Vote who you want to win by commenting on this video.

228
00:10:53,958 --> 00:10:55,791
I forgot to give you rewards.

229
00:10:55,791 --> 00:10:56,250
Huh?

230
00:10:56,250 --> 00:10:58,416
Rewards for getting into the Final 3.

231
00:10:58,416 --> 00:11:00,666
Another reward? I love rewards!

232
00:11:00,666 --> 00:11:02,375
So, what are the rewards?

233
00:11:02,375 --> 00:11:03,750
Anything you ask for.

234
00:11:03,750 --> 00:11:04,375
Anything?

235
00:11:04,375 --> 00:11:05,666
Absolutely everything.

236
00:11:05,666 --> 00:11:07,458
Well, I wish for world peace!

237
00:11:07,458 --> 00:11:08,208
Wish granted.

238
00:11:08,500 --> 00:11:09,958
But y-you didn't do anything!

239
00:11:09,958 --> 00:11:13,458
I think the world is peaceful enough.
Moving on, Bubble.

240
00:11:13,458 --> 00:11:15,125
I want some yoylecake!

241
00:11:15,125 --> 00:11:20,458
Ooh, Sorry, Bubble, but that doesn't fit our budget.
Wish denied, onto Firey.

242
00:11:20,458 --> 00:11:22,708
I want my life's earnings back!

243
00:11:22,708 --> 00:11:24,666
Sorry, I already spent it.

244
00:11:24,666 --> 00:11:25,375
On what?

245
00:11:25,375 --> 00:11:26,958
Your new recovery centers.

246
00:11:26,958 --> 00:11:31,666
Wow, thanks! Wait, you didn't buy these
because you care about us, did you?

247
00:11:31,708 --> 00:11:32,083
Nope.

248
00:11:32,083 --> 00:11:33,375
Gasp! Then why'd you do it?!

249
00:11:33,458 --> 00:11:34,500
So I can do this,

250
00:11:34,791 --> 00:11:35,291
and this,

251
00:11:36,041 --> 00:11:36,541
and this.

252
00:11:39,375 --> 00:11:40,041
What's this?